            0.176,
            0.249,
            0.478,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "Note: Think of more such examples."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.275,
            0.881,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": "**Q.4. Find the remainders obtained when each of the following numbers are divided by i) 10, ii) 5, iii) 2.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.319,
            0.445,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": "**78, 99, 173, 572, 980, 1111, 2345**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.348,
            0.161,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": "Ans."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.373,
            0.937,
            0.524
          ],
          "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">Numbers</td><td rowspan=\"2\">a) Remainder when divided by 10</td><td rowspan=\"2\">b) Remainder when divided by 5</td><td rowspan=\"2\">c) Remainder when divided by 2</td></tr><tr></tr><tr><td>78</td><td>8</td><td>3</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>99</td><td>9</td><td>4</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>173</td><td>3</td><td>3</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>572</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>980</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>1111</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2345</td><td>5</td><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table>",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_32_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.551,
            0.883,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "**Q.5. The teacher asked if 14560 is divisible by all of 2, 4, 5, 8 and 10. Guna checked for divisibility of 14560 by only two of these numbers and then declared that it was also divisible by all of them. What could those two numbers be?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.614,
            0.883,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": "Ans. The two numbers that are sufficient to declare the divisibility of 14560 by 2, 4, 5, 8 and 10 are 5 and 8."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.658,
            0.883,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": "**Q.6. Which of the following numbers are divisible by all of 2, 4, 5, 8 and 10: 572, 2352, 5600, 6000, 77622160.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.704,
            0.56,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": "Ans. The numbers divisible by 2, 4, 5, 8 and 10 are: 5600, 6000 and 77622160."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.758,
            0.882,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": "**Q.7. Write two numbers whose product is 10000. The two numbers should not have 0 as their unit digit.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.803,
            0.333,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": "Ans. 10000 = 16 × 625."
        },
